latform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","02.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":233,"path":234,"stem":235,"icon":236},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","02.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":238,"title":148,"body":239,"description":563,"extension":564,"links":565,"meta":566,"navigation":567,"path":149,"seo":568,"stem":150,"__hash__":569},"docs\u002F02.platform\u002F01.architecture.md",{"type":240,"value":241,"toc":554},"minimark",[242,246,250,254,318,326,330,398,402,405,415,421,426,437,482,488,492,514,547,550],[243,244,25],"h2",{"id":245},"overview",[247,248,249],"p",{},"Kinotic OS is a full-stack application platform that handles service communication, persistence, authentication, authorization, deployment, and observability. The system is composed of several core components that work together to provide a seamless development and runtime experience.",[243,251,253],{"id":252},"core-components","Core Components",[255,256,257,274,287,300,306,312],"ul",{},[258,259,260,264,265,269,270,273],"li",{},[261,262,263],"strong",{},"Management server"," (",[266,267,268],"code",{},"kinotic-server-management",") — The API the portal, the Kinotic CLI and organization members' MCP hosts call: sign-up, logins and invitations, the ",[266,271,272],{},"management-api"," services, and the GitHub App's webhook.",[258,275,276,264,279,282,283,286],{},[261,277,278],{},"System server",[266,280,281],{},"kinotic-server-system",") — The API the system console and the vm-managers call: the ",[266,284,285],{},"system-api"," services, project deployments, and the cluster singletons that reconcile deployments and delete old workload runs.",[258,288,289,264,292,295,296,299],{},[261,290,291],{},"App server",[266,293,294],{},"kinotic-server-app",") — The API every application's users, UIs and microservices call: the ",[266,297,298],{},"app-api"," persistence services and the services applications publish in their own zones, each application at its own API host.",[258,301,302,305],{},[261,303,304],{},"RPC Gateway"," — Each server's gateway routes remote procedure calls between its clients and published services over STOMP\u002FWebSocket, and serves the server's REST and MCP endpoints.",[258,307,308,311],{},[261,309,310],{},"Persistence Layer"," — Provides automatic CRUD operations for entities backed by Elasticsearch.",[258,313,314,317],{},[261,315,316],{},"Auth System"," — Handles authentication (email\u002Fpassword and OIDC) across three authorization hierarchies: System, Organization, and Application. Each server admits only the participants it serves.",[247,319,320,321,325],{},"The three servers are Spring Boot applications that form one Ignite cluster, in which each hosts only its own zones. ",[322,323,172],"a",{"href":324},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fdefense-in-depth#network-architecture"," shows which participants each admits and which zones each hosts.",[243,327,329],{"id":328},"tech-stack","Tech Stack",[331,332,333,346],"table",{},[334,335,336],"thead",{},[337,338,339,343],"tr",{},[340,341,342],"th",{},"Component",[340,344,345],{},"Technology",[347,348,349,358,366,374,382,390],"tbody",{},[337,350,351,355],{},[352,353,354],"td",{},"Orchestration",[352,356,357],{},"Kubernetes",[337,359,360,363],{},[352,361,362],{},"Build Isolation",[352,364,365],{},"Firecracker VMs",[337,367,368,371],{},[352,369,370],{},"Runtime",[352,372,373],{},"Bun",[337,375,376,379],{},[352,377,378],{},"Search\u002FPersistence",[352,380,381],{},"Elasticsearch",[337,383,384,387],{},[352,385,386],{},"Logging",[352,388,389],{},"Grafana Loki",[337,391,392,395],{},[352,393,394],{},"Payments",[352,396,397],{},"Stripe Connect",[243,399,401],{"id":400},"communication","Communication",[247,403,404],{},"Services communicate via STOMP over WebSocket, with messages routed by CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier). Each service, method, and event stream is addressable through a CRI, which follows the format:",[406,407,412],"pre",{"className":408,"code":410,"language":411},[409],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[266,413,410],{"__ignoreMap":414},"",[247,416,417,418,420],{},"The RPC gateway uses CRIs to route requests to the correct service instance, apply versioning, and enforce scope-based multi-tenancy. See the ",[322,419,205],{"href":206}," reference for details.",[422,423,425],"h3",{"id":424},"kinotic-rpc-on-its-own","Kinotic RPC on its own",[247,427,428,429,432,433,436],{},"Kinotic RPC, the service and event layer in ",[266,430,431],{},"kinotic-core"," and ",[266,434,435],{},"kinotic-api-gateway",", runs without the rest of\nKinotic OS. A server built on it alone supplies two beans the gateway authenticates and authorizes every\nconnection with:",[331,438,439,449],{},[334,440,441],{},[337,442,443,446],{},[340,444,445],{},"Bean",[340,447,448],{},"What it decides",[347,450,451,464],{},[337,452,453,458],{},[352,454,455],{},[266,456,457],{},"SecurityService",[352,459,460,461],{},"Who a connection is: it authenticates the STOMP CONNECT headers and returns the connection's ",[266,462,463],{},"Participant",[337,465,466,471],{},[352,467,468],{},[266,469,470],{},"ZoneRulesResolver",[352,472,473,474,477,478,481],{},"What that participant may address: the ",[266,475,476],{},"ZoneRules"," of zones it may send to and subscribe in, which the gateway narrows to the zones the server's ",[266,479,480],{},"ZonePartitioningService"," serves",[247,483,484,485,487],{},"Kinotic OS's servers supply each from their own module: the ",[266,486,457],{}," of the server, and kinotic-domain's\nresolver, which gives system, organization and application participants their zones.",[422,489,491],{"id":490},"never-block-the-event-loop","Never block the event loop",[247,493,494,495,498,499,502,503,502,506,509,510,513],{},"A Java service published with ",[266,496,497],{},"@Publish"," is invoked on a Vert.x event loop it shares with the other services on the node, the same rule Vert.x sets for its own handlers. A method returns a ",[266,500,501],{},"Future",", ",[266,504,505],{},"CompletableFuture",[266,507,508],{},"Mono"," or ",[266,511,512],{},"Flux"," and lets the work complete off the loop; a method that is slow, because it blocks on a synchronous client, a lock or a sleep, or because it does heavy CPU work, hands that work off inside itself:",[406,515,519],{"className":516,"code":517,"language":518,"meta":414,"style":414},"language-java shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","@Override\npublic Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n}\n","java",[266,520,521,529,535,541],{"__ignoreMap":414},[522,523,526],"span",{"class":524,"line":525},"line",1,[522,527,528],{},"@Override\n",[522,530,532],{"class":524,"line":531},2,[522,533,534],{},"public Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n",[522,536,538],{"class":524,"line":537},3,[522,539,540],{},"    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n",[522,542,544],{"class":524,"line":543},4,[522,545,546],{},"}\n",[247,548,549],{},"The platform never hands off on a service's behalf. A method that blocks stalls every service sharing its loop, and Vert.x's blocked-thread checker reports it in the log.",[551,552,553],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":414,"searchDepth":531,"depth":531,"links":555},[556,557,558,559],{"id":245,"depth":531,"text":25},{"id":252,"depth":531,"text":253},{"id":328,"depth":531,"text":329},{"id":400,"depth":531,"text":401,"children":560},[561,562],{"id":424,"depth":537,"text":425},{"id":490,"depth":537,"text":491},"High-level architecture of the Kinotic OS platform.","md",null,{},{"icon":151},{"title":148,"description":563},"LyTcLpdaKIK3LdapE2eNvitWezEYWTSZZaRR9IYI6dA",[571,573],{"title":139,"path":140,"stem":141,"description":572,"icon":60,"children":-1},"Complete SQL grammar reference for migration scripts.",{"title":153,"path":154,"stem":155,"description":574,"icon":6,"children":-1},"Deploying and operating Kinotic OS in various environments.",1792928915032]